{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1541090472,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNzY0NzI5NDA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2967","origin":"github"},"title":"Make uninstall uninstall top-level datasets","message":"I think we had that discussion at some point but I do not think we have an explicit issue.  I think that API should become a bit more \"symmetric\".  We already can `drop` what we `get`, `remove` what we `add`, and IMHO we should be able to `uninstall` what we `install`.  But that is not the case ATM with top level datasets:\n\n```shell\n$\u003e datalad install https://github.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds001499\n[INFO   ] Cloning https://github.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds001499 [1 other candidates] into '/mnt/btrfs/scrap/tmp/openneuro/ds001499' \ninstall(ok): /mnt/btrfs/scrap/tmp/openneuro/ds001499 (dataset)\n\n$\u003e datalad uninstall ds001499 \nuninstall(error): /mnt/btrfs/scrap/tmp/openneuro/ds001499 (dataset) [will not uninstall top-level dataset (consider `remove` command)]\n```\nand I cannot recall the original motivation for having it so (IIRC it was very much intentional).","files":null}]}